    "q-276040": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276040",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "An unfair coin has an $80%$ chance of landing on heads. The coin is tossed $5$ times. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability that the coin landed on heads at least four times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin landed on heads.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=5$ tosses.\n\n- The probability of landing on heads is $p=80%=0.8.$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,0.8).$ \n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.8)^{x}(1-0.8)^{5-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.8)^{x}(0.2)^{5-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that the coin landed on heads at least $4$ of the $5$ games. So, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4})(0.8)^{4}(1-0.8)^{5-4}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5})(0.8)^{5}(1-0.8)^{5-5} \\\\  & =5(0.8)^{4}(0.2)+1(0.8)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.737,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
